graphql-intro-001.example:
```graphql
# A client asks for exactly these fields and nothing more.
query {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
    posts {
      title
    }
  }
}
```

graphql-intro-002.example:
```js
// Every GraphQL request hits the same URL; the body carries the query.
await fetch('https://api.example.com/graphql', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    query: `{ user(id: "1") { name email } }`,
  }),
});
```

graphql-intro-003.example:
```graphql
# One request replaces a /user call + a /user/:id/posts call,
# and returns only the three fields this screen renders.
query HomeScreen {
  user(id: "1") {
    name
    posts {
      title
    }
  }
}
```

